01:02:24.970 --> 01:02:30.000
was garbing away there, did she say something about tottened throat?

01:02:30.090 --> 01:02:38.830
Clint down. Seems like this she did. Let's go tell him how lucky he is.

01:02:38.830 --> 01:02:54.200
Alright. This horse is gone. He's a trailing Injuns. Alone.

01:03:03.450 --> 01:03:06.170
They've been traveling since 2 o'clock this morning to dodge the heat.

01:03:07.020 --> 01:03:08.960
Must be getting near the river by now.

01:03:09.280 --> 01:03:11.960
Yeah, I will jump them when I get them across.

01:03:12.370 --> 01:03:14.160
You understand? You tell them.

01:03:18.660 --> 01:03:30.000
Traveling in a straight line?

01:03:30.160 --> 01:03:35.840
all night. Now are you satisfied that he ain't trailing no Indians, huh? He's running

01:03:35.840 --> 01:03:44.380
away all right. But why? Uh, Jim, I've been kind of thinking. Do you suppose there's anything

01:03:44.380 --> 01:03:50.600
in what Doc Gero said last night, huh? Uh, I've been a thinking too. Oh, come on.

01:04:21.440 --> 01:04:23.200
- All right, have your laugh.

01:04:23.200 --> 01:04:25.310
- That's what you followed me for.

01:04:25.310 --> 01:04:27.950
You told me a gal would get a hold of me someday,

01:04:27.950 --> 01:04:30.000
and you was right.

01:04:30.000 --> 01:04:55.930
don't you but he's got me so I can't even look at her with us without one to

01:04:55.930 --> 01:05:00.000
grab her in my arm that's why I'm running away from

01:05:01.560 --> 01:05:07.520
so that I can beat it.

01:05:07.520 --> 01:05:10.880
And when I meet up here in Sacramento, I'll have it beat.

01:05:10.880 --> 01:05:12.750
But she loves you.

01:05:12.750 --> 01:05:14.480
I know that.

01:05:14.480 --> 01:05:16.900
You mean that you're running away from her

01:05:16.900 --> 01:05:19.440
because you love her too?

01:05:19.440 --> 01:05:21.280
Yes.

01:05:21.280 --> 01:05:22.550
Why run away?

01:05:22.550 --> 01:05:25.010
Well, I've been thinking.

01:05:25.010 --> 01:05:26.490
She's right.

01:05:26.490 --> 01:05:27.510
I ain't good enough for her.

01:05:27.510 --> 01:05:29.960
I wouldn't make her any gal a fit husband.

01:05:30.350 --> 01:05:35.660
You know, Sonny, what she's been a-blamin' you for, she'd have been much righter to blame

01:05:35.660 --> 01:05:36.510
us about.

01:05:36.510 --> 01:05:37.400
Mm-hm.

01:05:37.400 --> 01:05:40.200
Me and Jim ain't treated you right.

01:05:40.200 --> 01:05:42.820
We've been lying to you.

01:05:42.820 --> 01:05:45.370
The railroad is coming.

01:05:45.370 --> 01:05:47.370
Freighters have only got a little while longer.

01:05:47.370 --> 01:05:49.580
Oh, times is changin'.

01:05:49.580 --> 01:05:52.180
And you'd better change, too.

01:05:52.180 --> 01:05:54.180
You mean to say she's reformed you?

01:05:54.180 --> 01:05:56.080
We ain't a-talkin' about us.

01:05:56.080 --> 01:05:58.030
Well, you'd better go back.

01:05:58.030 --> 01:06:00.000
We can't do nothing.

01:06:01.440 --> 01:06:02.440
And she can.

01:06:02.440 --> 01:06:03.520
Mm-hmm.

01:06:03.520 --> 01:06:05.440
Not another place we went wrong.

01:06:05.440 --> 01:06:07.040
She's all right.

01:06:07.040 --> 01:06:09.040
And you're asking me to go back?

01:06:09.040 --> 01:06:12.220
It's the best thing for you, boy.

01:06:12.220 --> 01:06:13.690
Well, what are you gonna do?

01:06:13.690 --> 01:06:15.690
Oh, never mind about us.

01:06:15.690 --> 01:06:18.150
That's funny.

01:06:18.150 --> 01:06:20.130
You asking me to turn you down.

01:06:20.130 --> 01:06:25.020
After the way you cared for me when I was young and weak, ah.

01:06:25.020 --> 01:06:27.020
And now that you're weak and old.

01:06:27.020 --> 01:06:29.030
Old, weak?

01:06:30.380 --> 01:06:32.370
Why are you...

01:06:32.370 --> 01:06:35.100
You insolent, young chubby.

01:06:36.180 --> 01:06:38.180
I can still let you...

01:06:38.180 --> 01:06:39.500
I'll beat you a minute.

01:06:40.580 --> 01:06:42.500
Take that gin off your face.

01:06:42.500 --> 01:06:44.020
Put it down, get him down.

01:06:44.020 --> 01:06:46.900
Hey, don't take that gin off your face, will ya?

01:06:46.900 --> 01:06:48.660
- Have you got enough? - Go on, get up.

01:06:48.660 --> 01:06:49.780
Have you got enough?

01:06:49.780 --> 01:06:52.020
Wait a minute, the engine.

01:07:19.480 --> 01:07:27.110
- Supposed to attack the trains from both sides of the river.

01:07:34.570 --> 01:07:59.060
It looks a little tired, George.

01:09:30.090 --> 01:09:33.510
No, sir, I'm staying right here.

01:09:48.090 --> 01:09:50.970
Telling us, we was old.

01:09:55.050 --> 01:09:57.330
Well, he was right about you anyway.

01:09:58.450 --> 01:09:59.900
You missed that one.

01:10:06.400 --> 01:10:09.700
You're shooting like a cross-eyed spore.

01:10:40.430 --> 01:10:42.470
and they're running, like I told you, Mr. Turkico.

01:10:42.470 --> 01:10:44.270
You tend to your own shoes.

01:10:45.070 --> 01:10:47.390
I can get more than you two old cripples put together.

01:10:47.470 --> 01:10:49.430
Yeah? Well, you cripple them, sonny,

01:10:49.510 --> 01:10:50.910
and we'll finish them for you.

01:10:52.710 --> 01:10:56.190
You got him!

01:10:57.400 --> 01:10:59.690
We'll make a real Indian fighter out of here yet.

01:10:59.690 --> 01:11:00.000
Huh?

01:11:03.000 --> 01:11:12.390
Get ready to be the sole survivor of another massacre.

01:11:12.390 --> 01:11:17.570
The Indians want to catch us while we're strict for the river.

01:11:17.570 --> 01:11:21.530
If we can only get together on to the other side, we got a chance.

01:11:21.530 --> 01:11:23.730
Frank, you see, to get the stock across.

01:11:23.730 --> 01:11:28.890
Jim and me will take some men and hold them off here as long as we can to cover the cross.

01:11:28.890 --> 01:11:30.000
Where's the girl?

01:11:30.480 --> 01:11:31.510
Come on.

01:12:00.800 --> 01:12:02.760
Cigars, candies, and peanuts.

01:12:04.660 --> 01:12:07.180
You ain't got no answer for that one, have you?

01:12:07.820 --> 01:12:10.370
In case you had funny bones going back on you, eh?

01:12:10.940 --> 01:12:17.850
Well, come on, Jim.

01:12:18.480 --> 01:12:21.840
You will admit, you will admit that that was a funny idea, eh?

01:12:22.520 --> 01:12:25.970
Cigars, candies, and peanuts.

01:12:34.830 --> 01:12:37.590
It was a funny idea.

01:13:04.350 --> 01:13:09.890
Here's one massacre you ain't survived.

01:13:38.160 --> 01:13:44.240
- Finish, Bridget Jackson.

01:13:44.240 --> 01:13:45.910
- You can't help me now.

01:13:45.910 --> 01:13:51.090
- Nothing will stop them.

01:13:51.090 --> 01:13:52.090
- Turn those horses loose.

01:13:52.090 --> 01:13:54.020
- We can get this kerosene across.

01:13:54.020 --> 01:13:55.260
- Turn them horses loose.

01:13:55.260 --> 01:13:57.270
- Them menus have gotta be stuck.

01:15:00.670 --> 01:15:03.180
Let's pour two of them on this side while we've got them split.

01:15:03.180 --> 01:15:05.500
All right, boys, give it to them!

01:15:05.500 --> 01:15:06.470
Give it to them!

01:16:49.070 --> 01:16:52.950
"Whosoever believeth on me shall never die."

01:17:26.970 --> 01:17:29.920
- What are they? - A couple of lumbermen.

01:17:30.220 --> 01:17:32.820
two or three of the largest storekeepers in a drugstore.

01:17:32.840 --> 01:17:35.730
A regular welcoming charity.

01:17:35.810 --> 01:17:38.500
Girls, what are you standing around like this for?

01:17:38.600 --> 01:17:40.600
I want you all to put on your best clothes.

01:17:40.700 --> 01:17:43.640
Myrtle, get into your black satin with the Spangles.

01:17:43.740 --> 01:17:46.640
Hurry up, Goldie, you want to look your best for these men, folks.

01:17:46.740 --> 01:17:48.840
Me and Edgar married Sacramento tomorrow.

01:17:48.940 --> 01:17:51.840
And me and Nathaniel thinking of doing the same thing.

01:17:53.550 --> 01:17:55.280
Get back in that wagon, get back.

01:17:56.180 --> 01:17:58.490
It was not my intention to come all the way out here

01:17:58.590 --> 01:18:00.000
to open up a matrimonial entrance.

01:18:01.370 --> 01:18:05.150
This will make the third sale I've made since we struck California.

01:18:05.150 --> 01:18:09.010
Seth Higgins bought one of them air prints less than an hour ago.

01:18:09.010 --> 01:18:11.270
Did you say Seth Higgins?

01:18:11.270 --> 01:18:12.120
Yes, ma'am.

01:18:12.120 --> 01:18:13.420
Well, Land of Ocean.

01:18:13.420 --> 01:18:17.970
Oh, boy.

01:18:17.970 --> 01:18:20.630
Well, Seth Higgins.

01:18:20.630 --> 01:18:21.600
You?

01:18:21.600 --> 01:18:28.690
Come on, dear.

01:18:32.940 --> 01:18:54.140
I come to ask you if there's anything I can do to help you get started in Sacramento.

01:18:55.320 --> 01:18:56.690
No, that is nothing.

01:18:58.180 --> 01:18:59.670
Well, then, I guess there's...

01:19:00.000 --> 01:19:06.190
There's nothing more to say except that I'm giving up scouting.

01:19:06.190 --> 01:19:08.290
Yes?

01:19:08.290 --> 01:19:12.520
With them two gone, it wouldn't be the same anyhow.

01:19:12.520 --> 01:19:13.920
I'm sorry.

01:19:13.920 --> 01:19:21.140
I'd be awful lonesome riding back east thinking about them and you.

01:19:21.140 --> 01:19:24.780
Oh, but you will be free.

01:19:24.780 --> 01:19:27.970
I've been thinking that over.

01:19:30.540 --> 01:19:33.500
I'd rather eat with a napkin around my neck for the rest of my life.

01:19:34.350 --> 01:19:40.690
Then, perhaps you will permit me to sell you some of my fine linen, huh?

01:19:41.840 --> 01:19:47.280
You've got it coming to you to have all the fun with me you want, but not now.

01:19:47.790 --> 01:19:51.130
I'm asking you a question, and the answer can't be maybe.

01:19:51.770 --> 01:19:54.110
It's got to be yes or no straight out, understand?

01:19:56.400 --> 01:20:00.000
Will you marry me?

01:20:00.000 --> 01:20:03.690
- Yes or no?

01:20:03.690 --> 01:20:05.890
- Oui, monsieur.
